Subject: Pass binary leaf values to the existing length validator

Management-common uses ytypes to validate generated YANG structs. The
binary branch leaves the value for validation unset, allowing invalid
binary lengths through. Forward the actual byte slice to the existing
binary validator so its original length checks run; retain the schema-type
rejection and all other leaf conversions.

Origin: SONiC shared-module correction exposed by the original ytypes
validation tests, not a change to the selected YANG length constraints.
https://github.com/securely1g/sonic-bazel-registry/pull/214

diff --git a/ytypes/leaf.go b/ytypes/leaf.go
--- a/ytypes/leaf.go
+++ b/ytypes/leaf.go
@@ -67,6 +67,7 @@
 		if ykind != yang.Ybinary {
 			return util.NewErrs(fmt.Errorf("bad leaf type: expect []byte for binary value %v for schema %s, have type %v", value, schema.Name, ykind))
 		}
+		rv = value
 	case reflect.Int64:
 		if ykind != yang.Yenum && ykind != yang.Yidentityref && ykind != yang.Yunion {
 			return util.NewErrs(fmt.Errorf("bad leaf type: expect Int64 for enum type for schema %s, have type %v", schema.Name, ykind))
